        "body": "A state is always a colour field and its topmark together. A new state indicator that shows colour without the mark, or the mark in a colour other than its state, is wrong.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Produced-State Rule",
        "body": "An operator action button wears the colour of the state it creates: Vendre = ticket yellow, Sortir = sortie blue, Retour = libre green. Never colour an action by urgency or brand.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Signal-Budget Rule",
        "body": "Saturated colour appears only on state, on state-producing actions, on the late alarm, and on the shell's yellow accent line. Everything else is neutral ink on white.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Same-Signal-At-Night Rule",
        "body": "The four state fields keep their day values in the dark theme; only grounds, inks, on-surface state text and the focus colour (to yellow) change.",
